    <bpmn:process id="W_W4041" name="W4041. Political-Engagement Stakeholder &amp; Relationship Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Engagement plan; relationship lifecycle
Frequency: Continuous
Volume: Multi-stakeholder (national, regional, LGU, regulator)
Owner: Government Affairs Manager
Participants: Govt Affairs (links to VS-104), Legal (links to VS-100), regional teams, B2G Sales (links to VS-46), Corporate Communications (links to VS-14.3)
Source: workflow W4041 — Political-Engagement Stakeholder &amp; Relationship Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4041_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4041_Lane1" name="Govt Affairs">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4041_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4041_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4041_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4041_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4041_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4041_Start3" name="Engagement plan; relationship lifecycle">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4041_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4041_Task4" name="Govt Affairs maintain the stakeholder/relationship map and CRM for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Govt Affairs maintain the stakeholder/relationship map and CRM for political-engagement stakeholders (officials, regulators, LGUs links to VS-76, associations links to VS-104.2), with relationship owners, interaction history, and conduct compliance (links to W4037 anti-graft and W4038)
Responsible (R): Govt Affairs / regional teams
Accountable (A): Government Affairs Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4041_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4041_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4041_Task5" name="Govt Affairs manage engagements per the conduct standards (links to W4037) and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Govt Affairs manage engagements per the conduct standards (links to W4037) and the lobbying/advocacy registry (links to W4028), ensuring consistent, accountable, and documented interaction
Responsible (R): Govt Affairs
Accountable (A): Government Affairs Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4041_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4041_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4041_Task6" name="Govt Affairs/Comms coordinate stakeholder messaging with corporate…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Govt Affairs/Comms coordinate stakeholder messaging with corporate communications (links to VS-14.3) and brand/reputation (links to VS-25), and report relationship health to leadership
Responsible (R): Govt Affairs / Comms
Accountable (A): Government Affairs Manager
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4041_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4041_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4041_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4041_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4041_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-628 (ensure controlled execution — Stakeholder &amp; Government Affairs Governance, Monitoring &amp; Analytics (PA-132.3).) | - operational: single owner and CRM; operational: conduct standards
Owner: Government Affairs Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4041_Assoc9" sourceRef="W4041_Annotation8" targetRef="W4041_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4041_Flow10" sourceRef="W4041_Start3" targetRef="W4041_Task4" />
